-**Lazy Kokoro TTS (2026-09-01).** Kokoro is no longer loaded at boot.
-`speak_text` calls `ensure_engine_loaded()` on first use — loads in ~1.7s
-(one-time), then stays loaded. Saves ~350 MB at idle. See `tts.rs`.
+**Lazy Piper TTS (2026-09-02).** Piper replaces Kokoro. Piper is no longer
+loaded at boot. `speak_text` calls `ensure_engine_loaded()` on first use —
+loads in ~85ms (one-time), then stays loaded. Saves ~80 MB at idle vs
+Kokoro's 350 MB. Model: `en_US-amy-medium` (~63 MB, 22050 Hz, MOS 4.0-4.3).
+Auto-downloads from HuggingFace on first speak (one-time). See `tts.rs`.
+
+**Self-Learning STT Corrections (2026-09-02).** When STT mishears a word
+and the parser fails, the user repeats the command. The system detects
+this pattern and learns the correction automatically. After 3 consistent
+corrections, the correction is auto-applied. Storage:
+`%APPDATA%/com.nexus.assistant/learned_corrections.json`. See
+`stt_learning.rs`. RAM cost: ~1-10 KB.
+
+**Fuzzy Repo Matching (2026-09-02).** When a PR command's repo name
+doesn't exactly match a known repo, the parser tries Levenshtein fuzzy
+matching against `KNOWN_REPOS` (nexus, ultron, servx, zync, ledger-ai,
+nexus-agent). Threshold: 2 for short repos (≤6 chars), 3 for longer.
+Fuzzy matches return confidence 0.8 and source "fuzzy". See
+`intent_parser.rs::fuzzy_match_repo_name()`.
 
